<section>
  <h2>Sample case-study structure</h2>
  <p>Every case study follows the same honest structure:</p>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li><strong>Client</strong> (with permission) or anonymised description ("a 60-room Dooars resort").</li>
    <li><strong>Challenge</strong> — the specific operational problem at signing.</li>
    <li><strong>Approach</strong> — guard count, tier mix, supervisor model, equipment, special protocols.</li>
    <li><strong>Outcome</strong> — measurable change in incidents, theft, response time, or client-reported satisfaction.</li>
    <li><strong>What went wrong</strong> — every deployment has friction. We document what broke and how we fixed it.</li>
    <li><strong>What we'd do differently</strong> — for ourselves and for similar clients.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

